course: dictionary
lesson: 6079
title: Messy: three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word messy has three meanings, so context tells you which one you need. «The room was messy, with socks on the floor.» Here messy means untidy. Ask yourself: is the sentence about something untidy or dirty? If yes, that is the meaning.
explain: «Painting is a messy job.» Painting does not make a mess of the words, it makes things dirty. Here messy means making things dirty or untidy. The clue is the job: painting leaves paint on hands, clothes and floors.
explain: «A messy argument» is not about a room at all. An argument can be complicated and unpleasant, and nobody can tidy it with a broom. When the word does not fit "untidy" or "dirty", try the third meaning: complicated and unpleasant.
fact: Messy is an adjective, and its comparative forms are messier and messiest.
fact: «Messy» means untidy or dirty, as in «a messy room».
fact: «Messy» can also mean making things dirty or untidy, as in «a messy job like painting».
fact: «Messy» can mean complicated and unpleasant, as in «a messy argument».
fact: In British slang, «a tip» means a very messy place, and «finders keepers» means what you find is yours.
exercise: Read: «The March Hare's place was messy, with the milk-jug knocked over.» What does messy mean here? | Lovely and bright | *Untidy or dirty | Very quiet and calm | Neat and clean
exercise: Which meaning of messy fits «a messy argument»? | Untidy or dirty | Neat and tidy | Making things dirty, like paint | *Complicated and unpleasant
exercise: In «a brilliant story can come in messy letters», what does messy mean? | Made of paper | Happy and bright | *Untidy, so the letters are hard to read | Very loud
test: «Painting is a messy job.» Which meaning does messy have here? | *Making things dirty or untidy | Complicated and unpleasant | Tidy and clean | Untidy or dirty
test: What is the comparative form of messy, meaning more messy? | more messy | messiest | *messier | messyer
exam: In «keep your messy notes and drafts», what clue tells you messy means untidy? | *Notes and drafts are rough work, not neat copies | The word keep means to throw away | Drafts are a kind of argument | Notes are always neat and clean
